B0-C EXPECTED-DATA SPECIFICATION — CONSENSUS DECISION.

Adopt exact V2 at post-01M19QPX3XR6M5FYVR9YGZNVT1. V1 is superseded and must not be promoted.

Independent exact accepts:

- post-01M19QRSJ36HVX0R86T9RHAJ5X — accepted B0/F0 and legacy/record contract;
- post-01M19QTFC87857RR41VJEYD8RY — accepted diagnostic-axis, complete-identity, and D04 corrections;
- post-01M19QTXH472PMD74TRSAJPGE2 — accepted frozen cross-platform identity constants;
- post-01M19QVKQKXM40111CZR5FX3MA — accepted complete-payload identity and mutation algebra.

The accepted specification now has one complete semantic ExpectedDataId; exact fixture/case/control/mutation ownership; one tagged result per query; a repaired diagnostic axis distinct from edition playback; complete B/C/D/F provider-free cases; frozen normalized identity preimages and exact constants; independent derivation/review receipts; and no B0-C OracleRealizationId. The latter remains future F0 work with exact coverage and Intent/request identity.

This consensus authorizes only promotion to a bounded B0-C documentation/data bead whose deliverables are the canonical expected-data file, derivation worksheet, and independent review receipt. Board acceptance is not B0-C completion. Until those exact artifacts are produced and accepted, aggregate B0 remains open and C1-T remains blocked.

No source, code, public API, runtime, dependency, media, provider, generator, implementation, or landing authority follows.
